  "Solution": "A is a linear function. B contains \\(1/x\\), so its right-hand side is not a polynomial. In C, the \\(x^2\\) terms cancel after expansion, giving \\(y=-2x+1\\), which is a linear function. D expands to \\(y=3x^2-6x+5\\), which is a quadratic function.",
